{#
  Base BGP peering in the DEFAULT VRF - the session phases 1 and 2 ride on.

  This is the CR an admin writes. OVN-Kubernetes does not replace it: when a
  RouteAdvertisements CR selects it (via frrConfigurationSelector matching the
  label below), OVN-Kubernetes reads the peering out of it and GENERATES a
  second, additive FRRConfiguration carrying the prefixes to advertise. Both
  exist; the generated one is named route-advertisements-* and should not be
  edited.

  nodeSelector is empty on purpose and must stay that way. In this lab only
  the workers have a fabric NIC, so narrowing it to them looks like the
  tidier choice - it is not. RouteAdvertisements with targetVRF 'auto' (the
  VRF-Lite and EVPN phases) checks, per node, that the FRRConfigurations
  selected for that node cover every selected network active on it. A Layer3
  CUDN is active on the masters too, so a master left with no matching
  FRRConfiguration makes the whole CR fail with "selected FRRConfigurations
  for node X don't match all selected networks".

  The price is that the masters hold a BGP session they can never establish,
  because the neighbor is on a fabric NIC they do not have. That is expected
  here: the session sits in Connect and the master's pod subnet is not
  advertised, which is fine because the lab's workloads run on the workers.
  Give the masters a fabric NIC as well if you want them advertised.

  toReceive mode 'all' is what makes the fabric's prefixes usable inside the
  cluster: FRR-K8s installs received routes into the node's kernel routing
  table, so a route to a tenant's external network learned here becomes a
  real route on the node. This is the mechanism that replaces the "point the
  UDN's default gateway at the router" idea - the pods' gateway never moves,
  the node simply learns where the fabric's prefixes are. The leaf's own
  outbound route-map still refuses to send {{ lab_network_prefix }}.0/24, so
  no BGP-learned route can ever shadow the lab's management network.
#}
apiVersion: frrk8s.metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: FRRConfiguration
metadata:
  name: fabric-peering-default
  namespace: {{ udn_bgp_frrk8s_namespace }}
  labels:
    {{ udn_bgp_frr_label_key }}: fabric-default
spec:
  bgp:
    routers:
      - asn: {{ clab_cluster_asn }}
        neighbors:
          - address: {{ clab_fabric_prefix }}.{{ clab_fabric_router_octet }}
            asn: {{ clab_leaf1_asn }}
            # Short timers so a lab session converges in seconds. The leaf
            # runs FRR's 'datacenter' defaults, which match.
            holdTime: 9s
            keepaliveTime: 3s
            port: 179
            toReceive:
              allowed:
                mode: all
            toAdvertise:
              allowed:
                # 'filtered' with no prefixes of our own: everything this
                # session advertises comes from the FRRConfiguration
                # OVN-Kubernetes generates off the RouteAdvertisements CR.
                # Setting 'all' here would advertise the node's own
                # connected routes, {{ lab_network_prefix }}.0/24 included.
                mode: filtered
  nodeSelector: {}
